From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:55:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 35/43] minimize: move the preview popup between items instead
 of recreating it

Moving the pointer from one taskbar item to the next destroyed the preview
popup and created a new one. cosmic-comp draws a destroyed surface for one
more frame; its texture is already released then, which logs "Failed to
render texture ..., import for wrong devices" (smithay clear_surface_textures).

The popup now stays for 100 ms after the pointer left an item; the next item
repositions it (xdg_popup.reposition) and the title is read on redraw like
the image. It is destroyed when the pointer leaves the taskbar, and recreated
when the parent surface changes (panel vs overflow list). The hover delay of
a first open moves from the tooltip into the app, which needs the popup
action itself to decide.

